IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rtw-dates`
IMPORT `rtw-core`
IMPORT `rtw-seat`

-- Return to Work Act 2014 (SA) -- cases for the injured worker's seat (rtw-seat.l4).
--
-- The illustrative worker is Mia, as in rtw-cases-core.l4: a full-time storeperson in Adelaide (38 hours a week), born
-- 14 May 1990, injured lifting on Monday 2 March 2026; incapacity first occurs on Tuesday 3 March 2026; claim given to
-- her employer (not self-insured) on Tuesday 10 March 2026; age pension age 67 (804 months). Others: a food delivery
-- rider, a carpenter and a cleaner on contracts, a minister, a footballer, a boxer, Peter (born 1 July 1960, injured at
-- 65) and Ben, who dies of a work injury with notional weekly earnings of $1,600.
-- ILLUSTRATIVE figures: CPI 125.4 for the September quarter before the adjustment and 100 for the base September quarter
-- (factor 1.254); State average weekly earnings $1,900; the Federal minimum wage $915.90 a week; prime bank rate 7.8%.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text, with the arithmetic in the comment above it.

§ `Am I covered?`

-- Mia, an employee: a worker.
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 5 classes` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100
-- A contractor in none of the reg 5 classes: not a worker.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 5 classes` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100)
-- Finding 1: a food delivery rider on a bicycle (reg 5(1)(e)): personally, for the platform's business, no employees, no
-- materials, one vehicle, goods not his or the platform's: a worker. Running two vehicles at once: not.
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `driving or riding a vehicle other than a commercial motor vehicle to carry goods` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `driving or riding a vehicle other than a commercial motor vehicle to carry goods` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100)
-- Finding 2: an employee who drives his own commercial van carrying others' goods is excluded by reg 6(4), employed or
-- not; if the employer supplies the van, he is a worker.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a worker` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 5 classes` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a driver carrying goods in a commercial motor vehicle the driver owns, leases or hires` 125.4 100)
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 5 classes` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a driver carrying goods in a commercial motor vehicle the driver owns, leases or hires` 125.4 100
-- A carpenter subcontractor on a $30 000 job: the materials limit is the greater of 4% (1 200) and $120 indexed (151), so
-- 1 200; $1 000 of materials and a $20 000 tool (limit $18 988 indexed, 23 811): a worker. $1 300 of materials, or a
-- $25 000 tool: not.
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `building work other than wall or floor tiling` TRUE TRUE FALSE 1000 30000 20000 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `building work other than wall or floor tiling` TRUE TRUE FALSE 1300 30000 20000 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `building work other than wall or floor tiling` TRUE TRUE FALSE 1000 30000 25000 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100)
-- A cleaner on a 3-month contract supplying $420 of materials: an average of $140 a month, within $120 indexed (151), so a
-- worker; with no indexation, $140 is over $120 and she is not (finding 12).
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `cleaning work other than window cleaning` TRUE TRUE FALSE 420 0 0 3 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `cleaning work other than window cleaning` TRUE TRUE FALSE 420 0 0 3 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 100 100)
-- A window cleaner for one month: $70 of materials is within $60 indexed (76); $80 is not.
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `window cleaning work` TRUE TRUE FALSE 70 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `window cleaning work` TRUE TRUE FALSE 80 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100)
-- A minister: reg 5(5) brings the work in "subject to regulation 6", and reg 6(1) takes out the named churches' ministers.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `the work of a minister, priest or other member of a religious order` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a minister, priest, pastor or deaconess named in regulation 6(1)` 125.4 100)
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `the work of a minister, priest or other member of a religious order` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100
-- An employed footballer is excluded (reg 6(2)); a boxer engaged for a fee is not (reg 6(3)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a worker` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 5 classes` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a contestant employed for a sporting or athletic activity` 125.4 100)
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 5 classes` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a contestant who is a licensed race rider or driver, or a boxer or wrestler engaged for a fee` 125.4 100
-- s 4(2): employed fishing crew paid by a share are not workers. A CFS volunteer is (Schedule 1).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a worker` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 5 classes` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100)
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 5 classes` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100
-- s 4(4), reg 5(8): the principal is taken to be the employer only if the contractor is not registered.
#ASSERT `Is the principal taken to be my employer` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the principal taken to be my employer` TRUE TRUE)

-- s 7: Mia's back, lifting at work: a work injury.
#ASSERT `Is my injury a work injury` `a physical injury` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A psychiatric injury mainly from reasonable performance management (s 7(4)): not; from bullying: yes.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my injury a work injury` `a psychiatric injury` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is my injury a work injury` `a psychiatric injury` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 7(7): hurt at the Christmas party, not part of the job and not at the employer's request: not; at its request: yes.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my injury a work injury` `a physical injury` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is my injury a work injury` `a physical injury` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 7(8)-(10): on the direct way home with a real and substantial connection to work: yes; with no such connection (s 7(9):
-- the accident on the way home is not enough): no; with a substantial riskier deviation: no.
#ASSERT `Is my injury a work injury` `a physical injury` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my injury a work injury` `a physical injury` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my injury a work injury` `a physical injury` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Finding 4 (READING): a journey in the course of duties still needs the real and substantial connection.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my injury a work injury` `a physical injury` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Notice and claim`

#ASSERT `To whom must I give notice of my injury` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the employer by whom the worker was employed when the injury occurred`
#ASSERT `To whom must I give notice of my injury` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Corporation`
#ASSERT `Within how many hours should I give notice of my injury` TRUE 0 EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `Within how many hours should I give notice of my injury` FALSE 72 EQUALS 72
#ASSERT `Is my notice taken to have been given to my employer` `to the person who supervised the worker when the injury occurred`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my notice taken to have been given to my employer` `in some other way`)
-- s 30(10): 6 months commencing 3 March 2026 end on 2 September 2026; commencing 31 August 2026, on 28 February 2027.
#ASSERT `What is the last day to make my claim` (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 2 9 2026
#ASSERT `What is the last day to make my claim` (`the calendar date` 31 8 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 28 2 2027
-- Mia claims on 10 March, having given notice: the claim may be made.
#ASSERT `Can I still make my claim` (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the claim may be made`
-- On 3 September, a day late: excused if the determination is not substantially prejudiced, or the delay came from absence
-- from the State; otherwise barred.
#ASSERT `Can I still make my claim` (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 3 9 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the claim may be made: s 30(3) excuses the lateness or the want of notice`
#ASSERT `Can I still make my claim` (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 3 9 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the claim may be made: s 30(3) excuses the lateness or the want of notice`
#ASSERT `Can I still make my claim` (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 3 9 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `barred: the claim is late and s 30(3)(b) does not excuse it`
-- No notice at all: excused by ignorance; otherwise barred (s 30(2)).
#ASSERT `Can I still make my claim` (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the claim may be made: s 30(3) excuses the lateness or the want of notice`
#ASSERT `Can I still make my claim` (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `barred: notice of the injury was not given and s 30(3)(a) does not excuse it`
#ASSERT `To whom must I give my claim` TRUE EQUALS `the employer`
#ASSERT `To whom must I give my claim` FALSE EQUALS `the Corporation, not the employer`
#ASSERT `Who can certify my claim` `a recognised health practitioner` EQUALS `a designated person may certify the claim`
#ASSERT `Who can certify my claim` `someone else` EQUALS `not a designated person`
-- s 30(5): received Tuesday 10 March 2026; forward by Tuesday 17 March. Not employed when incapacitated: no forwarding, the
-- claim goes to ReturnToWorkSA. A self-insured employer: no duty.
#ASSERT `By when must my employer forward my claim` TRUE (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) 0 FALSE EQUALS `the employer must forward it to the Corporation no later than` (`the calendar date` 17 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must my employer forward my claim` FALSE (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) 0 FALSE EQUALS `no duty to forward: the claim is given to the Corporation, not the employer`
#ASSERT `By when must my employer forward my claim` TRUE (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) 0 TRUE EQUALS `no duty to forward: the employer is a self-insured employer`
-- ss 31(4), 32(2): received Tuesday 17 March 2026: Tuesday 31 March. Received Monday 30 March 2026, with Good Friday (3
-- April) and Easter Monday (6 April): Wednesday 15 April.
#ASSERT `By when should my income support claim be decided` (`the calendar date` 17 3 2026) 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 31 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when should my income support claim be decided` (`the calendar date` 30 3 2026) 2 EQUALS `the calendar date` 15 4 2026

§ `Weekly payments`

-- s 5: Mia: 65 000 / 52 = 1 250, + 50 non-cash (a car) + 100 overtime component = 1 400.
#ASSERT `What are my average weekly earnings` 65000 52 50 TRUE 100 TRUE 1000 FALSE 38 38 915.90 1900 EQUALS 1400
-- A part-timer (20 of 38 hours) averaging 400: raised to the pro-rata minimum wage, 915.90 x 52.6% = 481.7634.
#ASSERT `What are my average weekly earnings` 20800 52 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 20 38 915.90 1900 EQUALS 481.7634
-- The same with an award wage of 500: 500 (above the pro-rata minimum).
#ASSERT `What are my average weekly earnings` 20800 52 0 FALSE 0 TRUE 500 FALSE 20 38 915.90 1900 EQUALS 500
-- A worker new to permanent work (s 5(4)): 36 000 over 24 weeks = 1 500.
#ASSERT `What are my average weekly earnings` 36000 24 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 38 38 915.90 1900 EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `What is my work capacity` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a current work capacity`
#ASSERT `What is my work capacity` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no current work capacity`
-- Mia, no current work capacity, NWE 1 400: 1 400 in the first 52 weeks.
#ASSERT `What weekly payment do I get` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) 1400 0 915.90 38 38 (`the calendar date` 14 5 1990) FALSE 0 804 TRUE EQUALS `the weekly payment is` 1400
-- Back part-time on 1 June 2026 earning 600: 800.
#ASSERT `What weekly payment do I get` FALSE FALSE TRUE (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) 1400 600 915.90 38 38 (`the calendar date` 14 5 1990) FALSE 0 804 TRUE EQUALS `the weekly payment is` 800
-- 2 March 2027, the second 52 weeks: 80%, 1 120.
#ASSERT `What weekly payment do I get` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2027) 1400 0 915.90 38 38 (`the calendar date` 14 5 1990) FALSE 0 804 TRUE EQUALS `the weekly payment is` 1120
-- 29 February 2028, after 104 weeks: nothing; as a seriously injured worker, 1 120.
#ASSERT `What weekly payment do I get` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 29 2 2028) 1400 0 915.90 38 38 (`the calendar date` 14 5 1990) FALSE 0 804 TRUE EQUALS `no weekly payment: more than 104 weeks after the incapacity first occurred (s 39(3))`
#ASSERT `What weekly payment do I get` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 29 2 2028) 1400 0 915.90 38 38 (`the calendar date` 14 5 1990) FALSE 0 804 TRUE EQUALS `the weekly payment is` 1120
#ASSERT `What weekly payment do I get` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) 1400 0 915.90 38 38 (`the calendar date` 14 5 1990) FALSE 0 804 TRUE EQUALS `no weekly payment: not incapacitated for work`
-- Finding 9: the part-timer on NWE 481.7634, in the second 52 weeks: 80% is 385.41072, raised by s 42 to 481.7634.
#ASSERT `What weekly payment do I get` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2027) 481.7634 0 915.90 20 38 (`the calendar date` 14 5 1990) FALSE 0 804 TRUE EQUALS `the weekly payment is` 481.7634
-- Finding 11: Peter, born 1 July 1960 (retiring age 67, 1 July 2027), incapacitated while employed on 2 March 2026; on 1
-- August 2027, after his retiring age but within his 104 weeks (s 44(3)), NWE 1 500, second period: 1 200.
#ASSERT `What weekly payment do I get` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 8 2027) 1500 0 915.90 38 38 (`the calendar date` 1 7 1960) TRUE 840 804 TRUE EQUALS `the weekly payment is` 1200
-- Until when: Mia, 28 February 2028 (s 39(3)); as a seriously injured worker, 14 May 2057 (age 67, s 44). Peter: 27
-- February 2028. A seriously injured worker born 1 June 1962, first incapacitated 2 March 2026: 1 June 2029.
#ASSERT `Until when can I get weekly payments` FALSE (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 14 5 1990) FALSE 0 804 TRUE EQUALS `weekly payments may be paid up to and including` (`the calendar date` 28 2 2028)
#ASSERT `Until when can I get weekly payments` TRUE (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 14 5 1990) FALSE 0 804 TRUE EQUALS `weekly payments may be paid up to and including` (`the calendar date` 14 5 2057)
#ASSERT `Until when can I get weekly payments` FALSE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 7 1960) TRUE 840 804 TRUE EQUALS `weekly payments may be paid up to and including` (`the calendar date` 27 2 2028)
#ASSERT `Until when can I get weekly payments` TRUE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 6 1962) FALSE 0 804 TRUE EQUALS `weekly payments may be paid up to and including` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2029)
-- s 41(3): an assessment on 1 June 2026; still paid as a seriously injured worker on 26 July (day 55), not on 27 July.
#ASSERT `Am I still paid as a seriously injured worker` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 26 7 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I still paid as a seriously injured worker` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 27 7 2026))
-- s 40, reg 26: surgery approved 1 May 2028; 15 May 2028: 1 120 x 140 / 135 = 1 161.48, up to 1 162. 31 July 2028 (91
-- days after): still 1 162. 1 August (92 days): none.
#ASSERT `What supplementary income support do I get` FALSE FALSE (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 15 5 2028) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 5 2028) 1400 0 915.90 38 38 140 135 EQUALS `the supplementary income support payment is` 1162
#ASSERT `What supplementary income support do I get` FALSE FALSE (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 31 7 2028) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 5 2028) 1400 0 915.90 38 38 140 135 EQUALS `the supplementary income support payment is` 1162
#ASSERT `What supplementary income support do I get` FALSE FALSE (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 8 2028) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 5 2028) 1400 0 915.90 38 38 140 135 EQUALS `no supplementary income support: more than 13 weeks after the surgery`
-- Reg 27: 1 July 2027 is a Thursday, so Sunday 4 July 2027; 1 July 2028 is a Saturday, so Sunday 2 July 2028.
#ASSERT `When is the minimum wage in my payments adjusted` 2027 EQUALS `the calendar date` 4 7 2027
#ASSERT `When is the minimum wage in my payments adjusted` 2028 EQUALS `the calendar date` 2 7 2028
-- s 43.
#ASSERT `Must I make reasonable efforts to return to work` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I make reasonable efforts to return to work` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Am I treated as making reasonable efforts` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as making reasonable efforts` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Am I a seriously injured worker?`

#ASSERT `Am I a seriously injured worker` 36 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `a seriously injured worker (s 21(2))`
#ASSERT `Am I a seriously injured worker` 34 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not a seriously injured worker (s 21(5))`
-- Psychiatric 30%: the 2022 transitional rule does not apply to psychiatric injury.
#ASSERT `Am I a seriously injured worker` 0 30 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a seriously injured worker (s 21(2))`
#ASSERT `Am I a seriously injured worker` 20 0 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `taken to be a seriously injured worker by an interim decision (s 21(3))`
-- Finding 10: a physical injury examined before the designated day.
#ASSERT `Am I a seriously injured worker` 40 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: the threshold for a physical injury whose final examination was before the 2022 designated day is not in the deposited text`

