§ `If a worker has died`

#ASSERT `Can the child be paid weekly payments` 17 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the child be paid weekly payments` 26 TRUE FALSE)
-- Ben, NWE 1 600: partner and 2 children in the first 52 weeks: 800 to the partner, 200 to each child. Partner and 4
-- children after 52 weeks: 100% cut to 80%: 640 and 160.
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does the partner get` 1600 2 TRUE EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does the partner get` 1600 4 FALSE EQUALS 640
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does each child get` 1600 TRUE 2 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does each child get` 1600 TRUE 4 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 160
-- Five orphans: 125% cut to 100% (320 each) in the first 52 weeks, to 80% (256 each) after. Two orphans: 25% each, 400.
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does each child get` 1600 FALSE 5 TRUE TRUE EQUALS 320
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does each child get` 1600 FALSE 5 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 256
#ASSERT `What weekly payment does each child get` 1600 FALSE 2 TRUE TRUE EQUALS 400
-- s 61 on 591 888: one partner and one child: 532 699.20 and 59 188.80. Neither: up to 591 888 at the Corporation's
-- discretion. One partner, no child, after a $58 807 s 58 payment to the worker: 533 081.
